      "strengths_deep_dive": [
        "Amoud Foundation demonstrates a commitment to financial stewardship by keeping overhead remarkably low. In FY2023, the organization reported <cite id=\"13\">$9,535,194 in total revenue</cite> while maintaining a <cite id=\"14\">program ratio score based on 89%</cite> efficiency. This financial discipline is paired with a <cite id=\"15\">leadership score of 69.25</cite> from Charity Navigator, indicating a stable governance structure that has supported the mission for <cite id=\"16\">over 25 years</cite>."
      ],
      "summary": "Founded in 1998, Amoud Foundation is a humanitarian organization dedicated to providing direct aid to vulnerable populations in Somalia and Somaliland. The organization focuses on <cite id=\"1\">supporting 15 orphan centers</cite> and specialized schools for the deaf and blind. In FY2024, the charity managed <cite id=\"2\">$11,142,566 in total revenue</cite>, representing a <cite id=\"3\">3-year revenue growth rate of 9.0%</cite>. This growth allows the foundation to maintain its core programs, which include <cite id=\"4\">emergency food aid, healthcare, and water projects</cite>. The foundation is <cite id=\"5\">zakat-eligible</cite>, specifically serving the categories of the poor (fuqara) and needy (masakin). While the organization maintains an <cite id=\"6\">overall score of 80.0/100 from Charity Navigator</cite>, it operates with a lean administrative structure. Its financial health is characterized by <cite id=\"7\">12.7 months of working capital</cite>, providing significant stability for its international operations. The charity's model relies on direct service delivery, ensuring that resources reach beneficiaries in high-need regions with <cite id=\"8\">minimal fundraising costs</cite>.",
